# DURABLE REPRO — an escaping closure that captured a local by reference reads
# a DROPPED STACK SLOT. `gg check` accepts it; both backends print garbage.
#
# WRONG TODAY (measured at HEAD, `gg check` -> "OK: no semantic errors"):
#     C     -> 281474467546264 / 281474467546264
#     LLVM  -> 281474641983928 / 281474641983928
# (ASLR-dependent digits; the stable fact is a raw address where 1 then 2 belong)
#
# `make()` returns a closure that captured `n` by pointer. `n` dies when `make`
# returns, so every later call reads freed stack.
#
# ⚠ THE DISCRIMINATOR, and the reason this slips through: the dangling-return
# check DOES fire when the closure RETURNS the captured value —
#     Callable[int()] make(): int n = 0; auto f = (): n = n + 1; return n
#     ...                    return !f          -> error[E_DanglingReturn]
# but NOT when the closure merely READS it (printing, here). So the check
# appears keyed on the closure's own return value rather than on what it
# captures. A closure that captures a dying local is unsound regardless of what
# it returns.
#
# INTENDED: `1` then `2` — the capture is by value, or the escape is REJECTED at
# check time with the same `E_DanglingReturn` its sibling already gets. Never an
# accepted program that reads freed stack.
#
# ⚠ THIS IS THE CASE THAT REFUTES THE "OWNER OUTLIVES" FRAMING. A closure can
# outlive the scope that made it, so a `&`-capture is precisely the boundary
# where the owner does NOT outlive the far side. Note also that EXCLUSIVITY
# cannot explain it: here there is exactly ONE writable path (the owner is gone),
# so the one-writer rule is satisfied and the program still dangles.
#
# ORACLE: ggdef cannot adjudicate — closures are outside the phase-0 subset.

void() make():
    int n = 0
    void() f = ():
        n = n + 1
        print(n)
    return !f

void main():
    void() c = make()
    c()
    c()
